[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m 
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m In v5.3, the `NDDataRef` class's mask propagation logic fails when an operand without a mask is used. This causes type errors when bitwise operations (e.g., `handle_mask=np.bitwise_or`) are applied when the operand does not have a mask. The issue arises because the current implementation tries to perform operations on an integer and a `None` type, which is not supported.
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m 
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m ### Solution
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m 
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m To address this issue, we modify the `NDDataRef` class to handle missing masks as follows:
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m 1. If an operand lacks a mask, we set its mask to `None` instead of applying the bitwise operation.
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m 2. This ensures the operation is valid and avoids the type error.
[36m(RolloutManager pid=91501)[0m 
